{
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "a01",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 2,
      "estimated_minutes": 2,
      "reason": "The description concerns where sale proceeds must be deposited under clauses (e)–(g), rather than whether face-value note sales qualify as Permitted Dispositions. Identifying that distinct complaint makes the comparison quick without resolving the separate § 2.6(a) question."
    },
    {
      "id": "a02",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 3,
      "estimated_minutes": 3,
      "reason": "One additional look separates the claimed conflict over escrow deposits and Account Debtor funds from d02’s inference of knowledge of MF08’s financial condition. The cited escrow provisions identify a separate routing problem, so their ultimate reconciliation is unnecessary to check the call."
    },
    {
      "id": "a03",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 3,
      "estimated_minutes": 3,
      "reason": "Although both sides concern the daily sweep, the description expressly challenges its compatibility with withdrawals and continuing account balances. The reviewer need only distinguish that operational conflict from the court’s question whether control of R.E. Loans’ funds supplied knowledge of MF08’s finances."
    },
    {
      "id": "a04",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 2,
      "estimated_minutes": 2,
      "reason": "The description targets the opening Subsidiary-formation prohibition and the definition of Subsidiary; d04 concerns the Permitted Dispositions exception for affiliate sales. Those separate words and problems are apparent without deciding whether the formation covenant is actually hollowed out."
    },
    {
      "id": "a05",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 2,
      "estimated_minutes": 2,
      "reason": "The description expressly connects R.E. Loans’ inclusion in § 5.1(c) with the Sponsored Investment Fund exclusion in § 5.7(e). That short, explicit connection makes comparison with d05 straightforward; the criticism of the protections’ effectiveness adds no separate factual inquiry."
    },
    {
      "id": "a06",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 3,
      "estimated_minutes": 3,
      "reason": "The reviewer must distinguish exclusions from the definition of Affiliate for Noteholders and certain fund members from the exclusion of loans to Sponsored Investment Funds themselves. The specified borrower categories make that distinction clear after checking § 5.1(a) against the court’s § 5.7(e) reasoning."
    },
    {
      "id": "a07",
      "difficulty": "intermediate",
      "score": 4,
      "estimated_minutes": 5,
      "reason": "Verification requires checking § 5.4(a)’s Loan Portfolio definition and the Offering Memorandum’s 'total Company assets' formulation. Once those references are checked, the denominator complaint is readily distinguished from d07’s question whether loans to R.E. Loans enter the capped category at all."
    },
    {
      "id": "a08",
      "difficulty": "intermediate",
      "score": 6,
      "estimated_minutes": 10,
      "reason": "The reviewer must separate the express Sponsored Investment Fund exclusion and reference to R.E. Loans from the broader claim that the exclusion may leave § 5.7(e) no operation. Checking the remaining covered borrowers and the lender-required co-borrower or guarantor qualification takes work before assessing how the bundled description relates to the court’s narrower construction."
    }
  ]
}
